{"step_index":84,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T12:47:06Z","content":"OK, the non-interactive mode isn't triggering the OAuth browser flow. Here's the reality:\n\n### The OAuth flow REQUIRES your interaction — here's exactly what to do:\n\n**Open your PowerShell terminal** and type these commands one at a time:\n\n```powershell\nclaude\n```\n\nThis opens Claude Code's interactive mode. Once you see the `>` prompt, type:\n\n```\n/mcp\n```\n\nThis shows a menu. Use **arrow keys** to select **nexlev**, then select **Authenticate**.\n\n**Your browser will automatically open** to a NexLev page that says \"Approve\" or \"Connect\". Click it.\n\nThen come back to the terminal — you'll see `Authentication successful`.\n\n**After that, type `/exit` to quit Claude Code**, and come back here. I'll grab the token and finish setting everything up.\n\n### Why can't I do this for you?\n\nThe `claude` interactive mode needs a real terminal with keyboard input for the `/mcp` menu. I can run commands, but I can't navigate interactive menus with arrow keys. This is literally the **only step** that needs you — 30 seconds, and then I handle everything else.\n\n**Go to PowerShell → type `claude` → type `/mcp` → select nexlev → Authenticate → Approve in browser → done!** 🚀"}
