{"step_index":88,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T12:48:01Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nWhat is this when I opened the Nexlev  ------- chrome://settings/content/siteDetails?site=https%3A%2F%2Fdashboard.nexlev.io                                      Location Access Required\r\nLocation is currently blocked for dashboard.nexlev.io. Allow it to unlock regional pricing — any of the ways below works.\r\n\r\nTurn off your VPN before allowing location access.\r\n\r\n1\r\nQuickest way\r\n\r\nWhen your browser asks to know your location, choose \"Allow while visiting the site\" in the popup.\r\n\r\nNo popup? Your browser has blocked location — use option 2 or 3.\r\n\r\n2\r\nFrom your address bar\r\n\r\ndashboard.nexlev.io\r\nFind this icon in your address bar\r\nClick the  icon in your address bar\r\nTurn on Location or go to Site Settings and set Location from \"Ask/Block\" to Allow.\r\nRefresh this page if pricing doesn't update\r\nor\r\n3\r\nFrom your browser's settings page\r\n\r\nCopy the settings link, paste it into a new tab, then set Location from \"Ask/Block\" to Allow.\r\n\r\nCopy settings link\r\nWaiting for access — this closes automatically once allowed\r\nSkip — continue with default pricing\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-08-25T18:18:01+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":89,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-25T12:48:01Z","content":"This is just NexLev asking for your location to show regional pricing — it's **NOT related to the MCP authentication**. \n\n### Just click **\"Skip — continue with default pricing\"** at the bottom of that page.\n\nAfter you skip that, you should see the actual **OAuth approval page** where you click \"Approve\" or \"Connect\" to authorize Claude Code to use your NexLev account.\n\nDid you already run `claude` and then `/mcp` in your terminal? Or did this popup appear on its own? The OAuth flow should come **from inside Claude Code** — not from just opening the NexLev website.","thinking":"The user is seeing a location access prompt from NexLev when trying to authenticate. This is just NexLev asking for location to show regional pricing - it's not related to the MCP authentication. They can just click \"Skip — continue with default pricing\" at the bottom to bypass this and proceed with the OAuth approval."}
